    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "1952782324392743402",
      "url": "https://x.com/QueenAleeey/status/1952782324392743402",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/QueenAleeey/status/1952782324392743402",
      "text": "TEN Tokenomics Explained.\n\nTEN Protocol’s Ethereum L2 drops a 1B token supply bombshell:\n🔹 13.87% circulating\n🔹 86.13% locked\n\nThis isn’t pump & dump territory, it’s a stability first play to keep value steady while building. Thoughts?\n\n> Those slick visuals aren’t just for show. \n\n@tenprotocol is powered by TEEs for confidential smart contracts.\n\nBacked by MIT research (Cramer et al., 2015), secure multi party computation = a privacy leap for Ethereum.\nScaling with secrecy? That’s next level.\n\n> Fresh from The Manila Time:\nTEN’s raise via Legion was community first equal access, zero insider allocations.\n\nThis flips the L2 narrative from VC heavy launches to user owned networks.\n\nCould this be the adoption catalyst? \n\n> Journal of Cryptocurrency (2023) found:\nTokenomics with > 80% vesting cut early stage volatility by 18%.\n\nTEN’s breakdown:\n43%+ to community\n\n6% rewards (50% instantly unlocked)\nThis is a slow release growth engine but will demand outpace the unlocks? \n\n> My take?\nTEN’s merging hard tech (privacy + scalability) with smart economics.\nNo live network yet, but the blueprint screams long game.\n\nSo, are you bullish, cautious, or waiting for mainnet?\n\nYour call. 🔟/🔟",
